# fstab.gex with /data kept from boot to boot: boot.sh binds this over the
# image's /vendor/etc/fstab.ranchu when DATA names a host directory, which
# gexc shows the guest at /gexdata. /data is that directory, bound there
# (fs_mgr takes `bind` as a mount flag), so what Android writes there (its
# packages' state, compiled code, settings) is there at the next boot, as
# a device's /data is; the boot after the first is not a first boot.
# The host directory keeps the files' owners and labels in its extended
# attributes (user.gex.owner, user.gex.selinux) unless gexc is the host's
# root. Remove the directory for a factory reset.
#
#<src>     <mnt_point>  <type>  <mnt_flags and options>       <fs_mgr_flags>
/gexdata   /data        none    bind,nosuid,nodev,noatime     latemount
